This module covers the basic concepts of Ethernet switching. I learned how switches work, how they forward Ethernet frames, and how they use MAC addresses to send data to the correct destination.

Topics Covered

Basics of Ethernet switching
How switches learn MAC addresses
MAC address tables
Ethernet frame forwarding
Frame flooding and filtering
How switches handle unknown destination MAC addresses
Unicast, broadcast, and multicast traffic

What I Learned
How a switch learns MAC addresses from incoming frames.
How a switch builds and maintains its MAC address table.
How a switch forwards frames to the correct port.
The difference between known and unknown destination MAC addresses.
How switches improve communication between devices on a network.

Practical Learning
I completed the Networking Devices and Initial Configuration course module on Ethernet Switching through Cisco Networking Academy.

Conclusion
This module helped me understand how Ethernet switches communicate with devices and forward data within a local area network (LAN).
